# Cloudflare Pages response headers for STATIC ASSET responses only
# (/_astro/*, images, fonts, favicon). This site is `output: "server"`, so
# every page route is rendered by the Advanced-Mode `_worker.js`; Cloudflare
# Pages does NOT apply `_headers` to worker output, only to static assets.
#
# The full security header set — including Content-Security-Policy — therefore
# lives in `src/middleware.ts`, which runs on every SSR response. Do NOT add a
# page CSP here: it would silently never apply to the pages it's meant to protect.
# The one policy below is not a page's: it is for a Web Worker script, which does
# take its policy from its own response.
#
# `nosniff` is the one header that genuinely matters for static assets: it
# stops content-type sniffing of scripts, images, and fonts.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# The BIDS validator worker (website#161, ADR 0028) is a static asset that runs
# as a Web Worker, and a worker takes its Content-Security-Policy from its own
# response, never from the page that starts it. So this header is the policy the
# validator runs under; the page's policy (src/middleware.ts) is not touched and
# gains no 'unsafe-eval'.
#
#   script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval'
#     The validator evaluates the BIDS schema's expressions, and compiles its
#     JSON checks, with the Function constructor. That is `unsafe-eval`. Besides
#     here it is allowed only on /dataset/* for the signal viewer (ADR 0009).
#   connect-src https://raw.githubusercontent.com
#     The one request the validator can make: a HED schema version it does not
#     ship is downloaded from there. Nothing else can leave the worker, which
#     makes "your files are not sent anywhere" a rule the browser enforces and
#     not only a fact about the code.
#   default-src 'none'
#     Everything else is refused.
#   Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
#     A worker sets its own referrer policy from its response too. The one request
#     the validator can make then carries no Referer, so GitHub is not told which
#     page of this site asked.
#
# test/bids-validator-vendor.test.ts pins this rule.
/vendor/bids-validator/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval'; connect-src https://raw.githubusercontent.com
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
